// case: generic-union-constrained-param
// what: n53 refuses a constraint on a model's parameter because the argument is
//      inferred and there is nothing to hold it to. A union's parameter is
//      inferred from the payload written for the variant, which is the same
//      promise about a value the compiler does not have, so `union Counter[T: int]`
//      is refused with the same shape of message and its own reason. The
//      parameter list itself parses -- this is the constraint half being
//      refused, not the brackets.
// expect-error: is not supported: a type parameter of a union is inferred
union Counter[T: int] {
    Tick(T)
}

fn main() -> int {
    return 0
}
